{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:61378",
  "title": "Important: freerdp security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-09-01 12:09:07"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-09-03 06:12:25"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "FreeRDP is a free implementation of the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP), released under the Apache license. The xfreerdp client can connect to RDP servers such as Microsoft Windows machines, xrdp, and VirtualBox.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Resource exhaustion due to oversized chunked HTTP responses (CVE-2026-67297)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Memory disclosure or denial of service via crafted RDP update orders (CVE-2026-67301)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via crafted smartcard cache requests (CVE-2026-67288)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via heap out-of-bounds read (CVE-2026-67291)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service due to RDPEI message processing (CVE-2026-67296)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via null pointer dereference in smartcard cleanup (CVE-2026-67304)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via integer underflow in RAIL channel handling (CVE-2026-67298)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Out-of-bounds memory access in Kerberos decryption (CVE-2026-73242)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Authentication bypass via incorrect RDSTLS PDU handling (CVE-2026-73241)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service and heap corruption via malformed RDP audio PDU (CVE-2026-63652)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Heap-buffer-overflow allows arbitrary code execution via crafted RPC response (CVE-2026-55194)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Arbitrary code execution via heap buffer overflow in Opus audio decode (CVE-2026-63633)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Out-of-bounds read leads to denial of service and information disclosure (CVE-2026-69159)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
